 "evidence": "Equilibrium tide of the atlas round's design surface's seas from Earth and the Sun, 2026-2045, every three hours, by geography/tides.py's model as it stands: degree-2 and degree-3 potential, lunar Love numbers k2 and h2 at degree 2, each sea's volume held, and the water's self-attraction to spherical-harmonic degree 60 with the solid Moon rigid under the load. A linear shallow-water solution on the near-side sea's main part, the salt sea and Smythii-Marginis checks the equilibrium for the eight leading lines. Each sea stands at its own level, so the seas' tides are independent of one another apart from their attraction.",
 "reading_rule": "As geography/results/tides.json: heights are metres of water level relative to the 2026-2045 mean; the monthly range is the highest minus the lowest level within an anomalistic month (27.55 days), its median taken over the months; the extreme range spans the whole record. Seas are keyed by their index into globe_surface.BODIES (1 the near-side sea's main part, 2 its southern seas, 3 the salt sea, 4 Humboldtianum, 5 Moscoviense, 6 Orientale, 7 Smythii-Marginis), each with the atlas's seas it replaces; statistics weight nodes by area. Stations stand at the sea pixel nearest each named feature, offset_km from it.",
